### Test /analysis endpoint (unknown field, Because StrictModel forbids extras, this should fail validation.)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/analyse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "My order is late.",
  "force_priority": "urgent"
}


### Test /generate-response endpoint
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "My order was due yesterday and I am frustrated because it still has not arrived."
}

### Exercise 02 case 1: valid customer + order pair (trusted context used)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "Where is my order? It should have arrived by now.",
  "customer_id": "CUST-101",
  "order_id": "ORD-1001"
}

### Exercise 02 case 2: same order under a different customer (no trusted context)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "Where is my order? It should have arrived by now.",
  "customer_id": "CUST-102",
  "order_id": "ORD-1001"
}

### Exercise 02 case 3: order ID without customer ID (HTTP 422, no Claude call)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "Where is my order? It should have arrived by now.",
  "order_id": "ORD-1001"
}
